Now game.js — the core. This will be long: state, UI, input, rules, loop, localStorage, menus, sound, AI.

Let's define the Game class.

Constructor:
```js
constructor(canvas) {
  this.canvas = canvas;
  this.renderer = new Renderer(canvas);
  this.sound = new SoundEngine();
  this.balls = [];
  this.cue = null;
  this.state = 'menu';
  this.inGame = false;
  this.menuOpen = true;
  this.players = [...]
  this.current = 0;
  this.tableOpen = true;
  this.isBreakShot = true;
  this.aim = -0.15;
  this.dragPower = 0;
  this.dragging = false;
  this.dragPointerId = null;
  this.spin = {x:0,y:0};
  this.ballInHand=false;
  this.handPos={...};
  this.handValid=false;
  this.shot=null;
  this.lastTime=0;
  this.msgTimer...
  this.profile = loadProfile();
  this.mode='cpu'; this.difficulty='pro';
  this.themeId = profile.theme;
  ...
  this.setupNewTable(); // rack for menu
  this.bindUI();
  this.bindInput();
  this.updateUI();
  requestAnimationFrame(this.loop.bind(this));
}
```
Menu table: `setupRack()` with players default, state menu; cue at head spot; menuAim=-0.18.

Start match:
```js
startMatch(mode, difficultyId) {
  this.mode=mode; this.difficulty=...
  this.inGame=true; this.menuOpen=false; hide menu
  this.players=[
    {name:'You',isAI:false,group:null,avatar:'YOU',coins?...},
    {name: mode==='cpu'?'Rookie' etc, isAI:true, group:null, diff}
  ]
  if mode==='local': P1/P2 both human
  ...
  this.current=0; tableOpen=true; isBreakShot=true; resetRack(); cue; ...
  entry fee handling
  state='aiming'; aim toward rack; timer...
  show turn banner; update UI
}
```
For menu vs CPU entry: if profile.coins < bet -> toast/menu warning and return. Deduct bet at start, store `entryPaid`. On win, add bet*2; on loss, nothing. If rematch via gameover, do we charge again? Yes, each match. Could deduct when starting. For simplicity: entry paid at start; if coins insufficient, disable. Rematch calls startMatch and pays again. If player wins 2x, net +bet.
- For 2P no coins.
- Player names: vs CPU 'You' vs named opponent (e.g., "Mika", "Rex", "Nova"); difficulty names. Could use "Rookie", "Rex", "Nova". Add avatars initials. Use AI name based on difficulty: casual "Riley", pro "Rex", legend "Nova". Maybe wins stats.
- Local: "Player 1", "Player 2".

Profile:
```js
{coins:5000, wins:0, losses:0, muted:false, theme:'classic', name:'You'}
```
Load/save localStorage. Guard try/catch.

UI elements IDs: we'll define HTML accordingly. Let's define IDs now:
- `#p1Card`, `#p2Card`, each with `.avatar`, `.p-name`, `.p-group`, `.p-target`? We'll set text.
