    - But if pointerdown happens near UI overlays, canvas didn't receive. Fine.
  - if state==='aiThinking' or shooting -> ignore.
- `onPointerMove`:
  - if ballInHand and (mouse hover or dragging): update handPos if allowed; for mouse, update on move without down. But pointer events fire on canvas.
  - if dragging pointer id matches: updateDrag(world).
- `updateDrag(world)`:
  - cue position. `dx = cue.x - world.x, dy = cue.y - world.y`; dist=hypot. Aim = atan2(dy,dx) if dist>6 else keep. Power = clamp((dist - 26) / 300, 0, 1). Should power map max at 300 world units. With cue at table center, 300 is 1/3 table. Good. Maybe 320.
  - We need `power = smoothstep`? Use `Math.min(1, Math.max(0,(dist-18)/285))`, apply ease `pow(p,1.15)`? Fine.
  - Set `dragPower`; update power UI.
  - Also if pointer is on the opposite side? Aim direction is from pointer to cue, correct.
  - Spin unaffected.
- `onPointerUp`:
  - if placing: if valid place cue; set ballInHand=false; state='aiming'; aim default toward nearest target or keep; update; play click; schedule AI if current AI (not).
  - if dragging: if dragPower > 0.035 -> shoot(aim, dragPower, spin); else cancel. reset power/dragging; update UI.
  - pointer capture release.
- For mouse hover in ball-in-hand, update handPos on pointermove even without buttons. On touch no hover; pointerdown+move.
  - `onPointerMove` if ballInHand && isHuman: update handPos regardless; if pointerdown started, okay.
  - On pointerup after placing: if state ball-in-hand, place on pointerup only if it was down. Simpler: pointerdown places immediately if valid? Then user can't drag to fine-tune on touch. Use pointerdown sets `placing=true` and handPos=world; pointerup if valid place. On mouse, click (down+up) places. Fine.
  - On mouse hover (no buttons), move handPos. On pointerdown while already hovering, sets same pos.
  - Note: pointerup fires after pointerdown even if moved; place at last position. Good.

Shot:
```js
shoot(angle, power, spin) {
 if state !== 'aiming' return;
 power=clamp(power,0.03,1); angle normalize;
 const speed = MIN_SHOT_SPEED + (MAX_SPEED-MIN_SHOT_SPEED)*power;
 cue.vx=cos*speed; cue.vy=sin*speed;
 this.shot = { ... , spin:{...}, spinApplied:false, context:{...}, isBreak:this.isBreakShot, startTime:... }
 this.state='shooting';
 this.isBreakShot=false; // for current shot
 this.aim=angle;
 this.sound.cueStrike(power);
 renderer.cuePuff(cue.x - cos*...);
 this.renderer.flash maybe;
 this.updateUI();
}
```
Context:
- player index/current, group at start, cleared (remaining own balls at start ===0), open.
- isBreak.
- Important: `isBreakShot` should only be true for the opening shot. Set false when shot begins.
- Hide hint, power resets to 0 after launch? Keep for a moment. Set dragPower=0.
- `shotClock` stop.

Update loop:
```js
loop(now) {
 const dt=Math.min(0.05, (now-last)/1000 || 0.016); last=now;
 this.time+=dt;
 if (state==='shooting') {
   const events=stepWorld(...); handleEvents(events);
   advanceDrops(...);
   if (allStopped && !this.resolveScheduled) { this.resolveScheduled = setTimeout? }
 }
 ...
 renderer.render(this, dt)
 requestAnimationFrame
}
```
Avoid setTimeout; use state timer `this.resolveAt = performance.now()+350`. In loop, if shooting and allStopped and now>resolveAt -> resolveShot.
- Need to let potted drop animations finish before resolve? Not necessary; resolve after 350ms while drop anim ~0.3s. Good.
- If balls still moving after 20s, force stop? Add safety timer: if shot elapsed > 18s, zero velocities. Unlikely. Implement.
- `handleEvents`: for each event:
  - hit -> sound.ballHit(speed, cue), renderer.burst at x,y with white alpha small? Maybe a tiny chalk dust at cue-object impact. Use burst 3 particles white, spread 30, size 1.2. For non-cue maybe no particles to avoid clutter. Add subtle.
  - rail -> sound.rail, renderer.burst with theme accent 2 particles maybe; skip particles.
  - pocket -> sound.pocket, renderer.burst at pocket with gold/white 10, spread 80; screen flash? Maybe small.
- Also update shot clock:
  - if inGame, state aiming, human, vsCPU, !menuOpen: decrement `shotClock`; if <=0 auto-shoot with power 0.32 along current aim, toast "Shot clock expired". Update UI ring text every 0.2s.
  - Pause while dragging? Actually timer should count; but a player might drag for 20s. Fine. Set 40s? Use 35s. Give enough. Maybe don't auto-shoot; instead it's just a display? But then pointless. In vs CPU, auto-shoot with 0.3. Implement.
  - AI shot clock not shown. Set 30s.
- AI scheduling:
  - After turn change/resolution, `beginTurn()`:
    ```
    const p=this.players[this.current];
    if (p.isAI) { state='aiThinking'; this.aiAt=now+900+rand; updateUI(); }
    else { state='aiming'; reset aim? Keep previous? Aim toward target auto. this.aim = autoAim(); shotClock=30; if pass-and-play show banner; }
    ```
