  - `.power-block { position: absolute; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); bottom: 4px; width: min(56vw, 420px); pointer-events:auto; }` with hint above power bar.
  - `.mini-stats { position:absolute; right:12px; bottom: 6px; display:flex; }` maybe hide on very short.
- `.stage { position: fixed; inset: 0; margin:0; border-radius:0; z-index:1; }` full screen.
- `.topbar { position: fixed; top:0; left:0; right:0; z-index:20; background: gradient; padding: 4px 10px; }` to overlay. But then canvas region under topbar; renderer must reserve top padding so table isn't behind topbar. Modify renderer.updateCamera to detect short landscape and use asymmetric padding: top 46, bottom 78? With fixed stage full screen. Let's compute: cssH=390. topSafe=42, bottomSafe=74, pad=8. available height = 390-42-74-16=258 → scale 0.403. Hmm worse than 0.355? No, 0.403 vs 0.355 better (13%). If bottom safe 52 (power bar 12 + hint 20), available = 390-42-52-16=280 → 0.4375, balls 10.5px. Better.

Wait currently stage height = 271 and scale 0.355. New: stage full 390, table fit height 280 → 0.4375. 23% bigger. Not huge but good.

